  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message as a potential self-identifier",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the bottom textual material ('i think ill skip my meds and stir shit up a bit') as a potential embodiment of the speaker or the person making the decision described. The meme's dark humor and the juxtaposition of Jack Nicholson's benign expression with the dangerous message invite the viewer to imagine themselves in the role of the speaker, creating a direct psychological projection onto the text. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' in the text, but the first-person plural 'i think ill' and the casual, self-referential tone strongly imply the user is being invited to identify with the speaker's internal monologue or potential action.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
